  "limits": [
    "Engineering fixtures establish mechanisms, not live benefit, live containment or independent human acceptance.",
    "No pull or merge request was opened on GitHub or GitLab itself: every forge request in this release's tests went to a local stand-in for GitHub on 127.0.0.1, and the repository's SSH remote reached a local bare repository through a stand-in ssh. GitLab's request path is covered by the existing forge unit tests only.",
    "The HTTPS push credential was checked through Git's own credential protocol (git credential fill), not by a push to a live HTTPS server.",
    "The token check is presence only: a token that is set but wrong, expired or without permission is found by the forge, after the branch is pushed; the page then offers Send again.",
    "Source review on the job page (carried from alpha.46, tagged at 657a45d and never published) was used once live, in the second real change on ZenJev on 2026-11-09, by Claude acting for Marc as a delegated agent; no independent human used it. That run used a build of its source before the alpha.46 cut.",
    "An exact earlier source-review decision offered again was exercised by tests only.",
    "Source-review decisions are operator assertions in cooperative-local state, not authenticated human judgements, and not a secret-free certificate.",
    "Each upgrade check started from every published release, so from alpha.45 and earlier: alpha.46 was tagged but never published, and no installation started from it. Each used an archive the tests run built from this commit, not the published asset, on GitHub runners (ubuntu-latest, macos-15). An upgrade on a person's own machine is not measured.",
    "A trusted-local delivery is still named contained-… in its records and its evidence commit message, because frozen records name it.",
    "The release run's artifacts were not downloaded; its job records were used."
  ]
